{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1474564-supernatural-twists-of-fate","id":1474564,"title":"Supernatural Twists of Fate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-13T06:43:08-08:00","id":1474564,"title":"Supernatural Twists of Fate","content":"In <b>Origin</b>, it's stated that characters with Legend can produce esoteric or even supernatural effects using the Twists of Fate mechanic: that is, spend extra successes from an otherwise ordinary roll to achieve an esoteric or supernatural result. What are the limits on this? Could you, for example, use Athletics rolls empowered by an appropriate Legendary Title to perform the sorts of feats featured in Crouching Tiger Hidden Dragon? Or would you need some Knacks and Boons to do that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T13:43:31-08:00","id":1474582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1474564-supernatural-twists-of-fate#post1474564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In <b>Origin</b>, it's stated that characters with Legend can produce esoteric or even supernatural effects using the Twists of Fate mechanic: that is, spend extra successes from an otherwise ordinary roll to achieve an esoteric or supernatural result. What are the limits on this? Could you, for example, use Athletics rolls empowered by an appropriate Legendary Title to perform the sorts of feats featured in Crouching Tiger Hidden Dragon? Or would you need some Knacks and Boons to do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>this is something I definitely need to discuss with writers and devs if I get the podcast my group is working on off the ground, because while you obviously can use a Legendary Title to perform superhuman feats by doing a Feat of Scale, what the line is between that and a supernatural Twist of Fate I am honestly not sure. It feels like a system redundancy to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T13:59:31-08:00","id":1474583,"title":"","content":"Actually, the distinction between the two is pretty straightforward: Feats of Scale are very specifically about, well, Scale: how fast you run, how hard you hit, etc. By contrast, Twists of Fate <i>don't</i> deal with Scale; even the supernatural ones don't operate in the realm of \u201cmore power!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}